# Frozen Lake ("Lake" on the panel; Crawl's third scene): the ice cracks (a recording and a note each), groans (the
# SAMPLE source, a tape loop on the chord's root), the keep's bell tolls far off, snow falls, meltwater drips; black
# keys run a crack, groan, toll the bell, send a gust, a drip, a flurry, make the ice give; each mood its own sound
# and picture: Grey Dawn still with the bell and a pale horizon, Thaw pools and drips and cracks thick, Whiteout
# the storm with the reeds singing, Black Ice the night with the stars in the ice and the groans
# (the simulator boots into Sakura; Frozen Lake is the last scene there: PRESETS one back)
wait 800
spin PRESET -1
wait 1500
expect scene 5
expect knob0 0
expect knob1 25
expect knob8 0
expect knob9 30
expect textfit 0
peakreset
wavgain 24
wav lake.wav
wait 60000
wavstop
expect lkcracks >1
expect scnotes >2
expect drones >0
expect nvoices <13
expect peak_db_max -27
expect peak_db_min -40
shot lake.png
# black keys: the first three a crack each (near, middle, far)
tapkey b0
wait 100
expect lkcracks >2
expect lknote 0
tapkey b2
wait 100
expect lknote 2
# the fourth: the ice groans (the SAMPLE source, part 7)
tapkey b3
wait 300
expect lkgroans >0
# the next three: the bell, one, two, three strokes; then a gust, a drip, a flurry, the ice giving
tapkey b4
wait 200
expect lktolls >0
tapkey b7
wait 2000
expect lkwind >40
tapkey b8
wait 3000
expect lkdrips >0
tapkey b9
wait 6000
expect lksnow >60
expect lkflakes >10
tapkey b10
wait 2000
expect lkgroans >1
expect lknote 10
# white keys: sixteen notes rising from 2; a crack runs where each lands
tapkey w0
wait 100
expect lknote 2
expect lastkey 2
tapkey w15
wait 100
expect lknote 17
# Mood (KNOB 1): Grey Dawn, Aeolian: still, the pad, the bell on its time, light snow, no pools, no night
spin K1 1
wait 500
expect knob0 1
expect scalenow 3
expect keyoff 0
expect knob2 0
expect knob8 0
expect knob9 15
wait 8000
expect lksnow >15
expect lkpool <5
expect lknight <5
shot lake-dawn.png
# Thaw, Min'yo three semitones up: the pools spread, drips, the monks, cracks thick, no snow, no bell
spin K1 1
wait 20000
expect knob0 2
expect scalenow 2
expect keyoff 300
expect knob2 1
expect knob8 2
expect knob9 70
expect lkpool >70
expect lksnow <5
expect lkdrips >1
shot lake-thaw.png
# Whiteout, In (Phrygian) a fifth down: the white, the snow driven, the wind high, the reeds sung
spin K1 1
wait 30000
expect knob0 3
expect scalenow 0
expect keyoff -500
expect knob8 4
expect lkwhite >85
expect lksnow >90
expect lkwind >25
expect lkgusts >0
expect lksings >0
shot lake-whiteout.png
# Black Ice, Hungarian minor a fifth down: the night, no snow, the groans and the whistles, one voice
spin K1 1
wait 25000
expect knob0 4
expect scalenow 6
expect keyoff -700
expect knob8 1
expect lknight >90
expect lksnow <5
expect lkwhite <5
expect lkgroans >2
shot lake-night.png
# round to Long Night again
spin K1 1
wait 500
expect knob0 0
# pixel art, and a new shore (another keep, other cracks)
tap GLO
wait 1500
expect style 1
shot lake-pixel.png
tap GLO
wait 1500
tap PLAY
wait 2500
expect regrows 1
shot lake-regrown.png
# back to the instrument: everything lets go, the instrument's own scale again
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 9000
expect mode 0
expect nvoices 0
expect par1 0
expect stale 0
